# HR role

| Product name | DB role id | Branch assignment |
|---|---|---|
| **HR** | `HR` | HQ sentinel → **All Branches (organization)** |

## Access

- Can use header **All Branches** + filter to one clinic
- Sidebar (exact order): Salary, Employee Database, KPI's and Performance, Attendance (All Branches + each clinic), Leave Management, Deductions & Benefits, Recruitment, New Hires, Resignation / Exits, Training
- Attendance: `/admin/hr/attendance` (all clinics) and `/admin/hr/attendance/:branchId` (e.g. San Mateo Attendance)
- Salary: `/admin/hr/salary` (All Salary) and `/admin/hr/salary/:branchId` (e.g. San Mateo Salary)
- Wired today: Salary → payroll, Employee Database → real employees + HR profiles, KPI's and Performance → `/admin/hr/kpis`, Leave Management → `/admin/hr/leave`, Deductions & Benefits → `/admin/hr/deductions` (recurring SSS/Pag-IBIG/PhilHealth + allowances; feeds salary), My Leave → `/admin/my-leave`, Attendance → HR attendance pages, Recruitment → `/admin/hr/recruitment` (applicants + interview pipeline + status), New Hires → `/admin/hr/new-hires` (auto from Hired + onboarding checklist), Resignation / Exits → `/admin/hr/exits` (exit interview + turnover checklist), Training → `/admin/hr/training` (upload materials + assign all/selected employees; employee completion on My Training for staff/clinic manager)
- Not full HQ (no marketing, warehouse, branch directory CRUD, user-access admin unless HQ)

## Implementation notes

- Frontend: `isHrRole`, `canAccessPeopleOps`, `RequirePeopleOps`, `hrNavSections`
- Create account: role `HR` → branch dropdown locks to **All Branches (organization)**
